    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_741deb178929d3be41bdd5902979a21c6df75ac5ecf1769ba06fd691b4bf3223",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Matching the smooth zero staircase does not generate its arithmetic fluctuations. An inverse semiclassical construction maps a prescribed density fluctuation into symmetric wiggly phase-space boundaries and then into localized waves, demonstrating where fine phase data can be represented; tested inverse-power level changes and prime-indexed deletions instead yield smooth arctangent responses and do not reproduce the reported irregular zero locations. Explanatory force therefore requires an independent law for the boundary phase rather than reconstruction from the target spectrum.",
