    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_9c45ca5b55fe0fe303f50f5b9728aeddfb70f121d9277201fc6f7ba574832d29",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Montgomery's Fourier-kernel interface makes the alpha<1 range a bandwidth limit: the prime Dirichlet polynomial remains diagonally controlled only while its length is below the averaging scale, and beyond that point the surviving off-diagonal terms regroup into shifted sums of Lambda(n)Lambda(n+h). A separate near-diagonal phase expansion of the zeta trace density reaches the same shifted von Mangoldt mean after compressing prime powers into Lambda.",
