    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_a2b8cabff563052b8023c6b317e57bf021381b15a05e057bc8133921a2010454",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Arithmeticity has two distinct spectral effects. Bounds under nonidentity field embeddings make allowable traces lattice-like; composing that count with trace-length growth yields large orbit-length multiplicities that can obstruct generic level statistics. Independently, an infinite commensurator supplies nonlocal Hecke correspondences commuting with the Laplacian, adding simultaneous spectral labels and identities useful for individual eigenfunction questions. These are parallel consequences of arithmetic structure, not a claim that multiplicity causes the Hecke operators.",
