    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_deaaef94ceb3dae6ba17d5f8f85ddf49de62fc3e19695f17c63defe020e5df63",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Hilbert-Polya requires a natural operator with an admissible domain and a complete discrete correspondence before spectral reality can constrain zeros. In both displayed Lie-Noether prescriptions, symmetry preservation reduces the PDE to fixed temporal exponentials multiplied by arbitrary functions of a scaling coordinate, making the residual continuum of amplitude data explicit. A separate formal-Hamiltonian audit shows why symmetry algebra and symbolic eigenfunctions do not replace boundary conditions, domain, adjoint control, and completeness.",
