      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A noncircular Hilbert-Polya route must define a natural space, operator, common domain, adjoint, and complete all-zero correspondence before self-adjointness can constrain zero parameters. The theta-weighted construction shows completed zeta entering through a chosen Mellin kernel while its operator is non-self-adjoint and its pairing is later replaced by a nonpositive zeta-valued map; the difference-operator construction similarly obtains Hurwitz-zeta functions through a noninvertible translation operator whose inverse needs a boundary prescription, while domain, completeness, and self-adjointness remain open.",
